hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1287","Narrated to us Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, narrated to us Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Kahmas bin Al-Hasan, narrated to us Bundar, narrated to us Yazid bin Harun, narrated to us Al-Jariri, and Kahmis, H, and Bundar told us, Salem bin Nuh Al-Attar told us, Saeed Al-Jariri told us, H, and Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Sulaym, meaning Ibn Akhdar, narrated to us, all of us in a whisper, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, he said: “Between every two calls to prayer is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer,” then he said in the third: “For whoever wishes.” This is the hadith of Abu Kurayb and Ahmad. Ibn Abdah, Abu Kurayb added: Ibn Buraidah used to pray two rak’ahs before sunset."
"1288","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Amir, on the authority of Anas, who said: “If the muezzin When the call to prayer is given, some of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stand up and go to the pillars to pray until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes out. And they also prayed the two rak’ahs before sunset, and there was nothing between the call to prayer and the iqama.” Abu Bakr said: He wants a lot of things."
"1289","From us Muhammad bin Yahya, from us Abu Muammar, from us from Abdul-Warith, from us from Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Muzani said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray two rak’ahs before sunset,” then he said: “Pray before sunset.” Two rak’ahs,” then he said at the third: “For whoever wishes.” He feared that people would consider it a Sunnah. Abu Bakr said: This wording is part of what is permissible. If it were not a permissible matter, then at the very least the matter would be a Sunnah if it were not an obligation, but it is a matter of permissibility, and I knew in More than once in our books, the command of permissibility has a sign when he discouraged an action, then commanded to do what he had discouraged, that command was a command. Permissibility, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, discouraged prayer after the afternoon prayer until sunset, according to the meaning that I have explained, so when he ordered By praying a voluntary prayer after sunset, that is a permissible matter, and God Almighty’s command of hunting when one comes out of the state of ihram is a permissible matter. It was forbidden to hunt wild game during the state of Ihram, due to the Almighty’s saying: Do not allow the game to be hunted while you are in a sacred state, Surah Al-Ma’idah, verse 1, and by His saying: And land game was forbidden to you as long as you were in sanctity. Surat Al-Ma’idah, verse 96. And by His saying: Do not kill game while you are in sanctity. Surah Al-Ma’idah, verse 95. Then when he ordered after the coming of the Message, By hunting wild game, this matter is permissible. I have explained this type in the book The Meanings of the Qur’an."
